91908ED264AD256D0006AC7FA2253A38,Bram Shano
91908ED264AD256D0006AC80BA37A0A4,An ISB report on Bram Shano.
91908ED264AD2B3100004BE16C9541A6,Ank Parako
91908ED264AD2B3100004BE2C54D80EB,An ISB report on Ank Parako.
91908ED264AD2D0500009D8E67ECF6F1,Asara Deyn
91908ED264AD2D0500009D8F04D14A37,An ISB report on Asara Deyn.
91908ED264AD6A4D00017880CC3982B9,"Bram is the owner and proprietor of The Broken Hoof, a popular sports bar in Canto Bight's Worker's District. Investigations into his affairs indicate that he's running a legitimate business but there are unverified rumors that he's involved with brokering robberies, bookkeeping rigged fights and races, and operating as a fence for stolen goods. 

These appear to be small-scale activities, and the ISB's primary concern in Canto Bight should instead be Wen Delphis and the Sixth Kin gang, which Bram is completely unaffiliated with."
91908ED264AD6A6B00017881C98A7323,"Ank has a considerable criminal record of robberies and other felonies, most of them perpetrated together with her now deceased husband Pirrip. With a criminal career spanning over twenty years, Ank and Pirrip were responsible for damages of over 590 million credits and were remarkably never arrested or detained. 

Thankfully, Ank's irresponsible behavior appears to have caused the end of her own career, as a botched vault robbery on Kijimi led to her capture at the hands of the Ashiga Clan. Investigations into this have revealed that Ank is working off her debts in the clan's weapons factory. Considering Ank's relatively old age for a Chadra-fan, it is unlikely that she will ever be released."
91908ED264AD6A7C00017882E55E3C31,"Asara Deyn is a verified member of the Rebel Alliance who should be considered a class 2 threat to the Galactic Empire. The ISB's investigations into Asara suggest that he grew up on Akiva with his parents and his sister Calys. Calys organized a local insurgency, and she managed to recruit Asara after making contact with a field agent from the Rebel Alliance. 

Calys left Akiva shortly after that and was killed months later in the Battle of Scarif. The ISB has information that suggests it was a tipping point for Asara, causing him to reach out to the rebel handler and join the rebellion in an official capacity. 

Evaluations of Asara's psychological profile suggest that the trauma of his sister is a strong pressure point that can be exploited upon his capture, and that it's likely that he will have access to actionable intelligence at any given time."
