D00CF65464C7D4A30000E053F4FFBC2A,Thieves' Quarter
D00CF65464C7D4A30000E05474034F39,Jet Kordo talks about the Thieves Quarter on Kijimi.
D00CF65464C7D4AC0000E05A13CB2509,Hutt Cartel
D00CF65464C7D4AC0000E05B03843160,Jet Kordo talks about working with the Hutt Cartel.
D00CF65464C7D4B70000E061DF7BC478,Chalmun's Cantina
D00CF65464C7D4B70000E062D60E2CE9,Jet Kordo talks about Chalmun's Cantina.
D00CF65464C7D4C20000E06E3617973A,Jabba the Hutt
D00CF65464C7D4C20000E06F73F7A433,Jet Kordo talks about Jabba the Hutt.
D00CF65464C7D4CD0000E075383FD203,Mos Eisley
D00CF65464C7D4CD0000E076CF7BBBF9,Jet Kordo talks about Mos Eisley.
D00CF65464C7D4D70000E07CD3932104,Tatooine
D00CF65464C7D4D70000E07D5062B5CC,Jet Kordo talks about Tatooine.
D00CF65464C7D4E50000E083694A9AFC,Tusken
D00CF65464C7D4E50000E0848A909CA2,Jet Kordo talks about dealing with the Tusken.
D00CF65464C7D4F10000E08A9006EEAE,Water Tax
D00CF65464C7D4F10000E08B9842755A,Jet Kordo talks about the water tax on Tatooine.
D00CF65464C7D4FE0000E09147D12077,Galactic Empire
D00CF65464C7D4FE0000E0926D7D2815,Jet Kordo talks about the rise of the Empire.
D00CF65464C7D50B0000E098867DCFB6,Kessel Run
D00CF65464C7D50B0000E099538784A5,Jet Kordo talks about the Kessel Run.
D00CF65464C7D5170000E09F8A1CB102,Pyke Syndicate
D00CF65464C7D5170000E0A02E5E2A55,Jet Kordo talks about working with the Pyke Syndicate.
D00CF65464C7D5210000E0A6422CDCE2,Jaunta's Hope
D00CF65464C7D5210000E0A76DFFC0A3,Jet Kordo talks about Jaunta's Hope on Toshara.
D00CF65464C7D5230000E0AD588596DB,Makal's Gambling Parlor
D00CF65464C7D5230000E0AEE3804914,Jet Kordo talks about Makal's Gambling Parlor in Mirogana.
D00CF65464C7D53A0000E0B41C8399B3,Mirogana
D00CF65464C7D53A0000E0B53CAC34BD,Jet Kordo talks about Mirogana City on Toshara.
D00CF65464C7D5450000E0BBFBEF5D65,Toshara
D00CF65464C7D5450000E0BCD4F20C5F,Jet Kordo talks about Toshara.
D00CF65464C7D5AC0000E0D84591EE47,"If you end up on the ISB's most wanted list, it's just a matter of time before they find you. There's no easy way to escape. The ISB have informants and agents everywhere, and those agents are true believers who will take you down with them."
D00CF65464C7D5BB0000E0DC79298D48,"The biggest mistake you can make in this business is working with rebels. They have no credits, and no matter where they go, the Empire is right behind them. There is no chance that outfit will amount to anything."
D00CF65464C7D5CA0000E0E061CE7955,"Akiva is fine, even if it's an old separatist world. It might get warm and humid but at least everybody minds their own business. And, best of all, the Empire is only there every fourth cycle."
D00CF65464C7D5D70000E0E425A5D804,"Myrra is great, when it's not under water. There are plenty of clients moving stock from there, and they keep a low profile. They are old timers, just like myself, because rookies who make mistakes tend to disappear in the jungle."
D00CF65464C7D5FF0000E0F078F85491,"The Alcazar is starting to become my favorite watering hole this side of the core. I could say a thing or two about the owner, but it is a solid place to get information. In this business, you do not get very far without information."
D00CF65464C7D60D0000E0F4AA19A396,"The separatists have an advanced droid factory underneath Myrra that produces an impressive amount of droids. The broken ones are dropped in one end, and moments later, new and shiny ones come out the other, ready to be deployed in the field."
D00CF65464C7D61E0000E0F8532FC0FE,"When dealing with the Ashiga you need to be aware that, even though they don't have eyes, they can spot a liar a parsec away. They have highly developed senses for pheromones and vibrations. The moment you try to fool them, they will cut you down without hesitation."
D00CF65464C7D62A0000E0FCB623CAAD,"The Ashiga are artists when it comes to gunsmithing, producing some of the finest blaster rifles in the galaxy. Their craft can make a fortune on the black market, but it is very difficult to get a hold of one. As always, the Ashiga want to keep everything to themselves."
D00CF65464C7D6370000E1002D7A2FD4,"Crimson Dawn is an interesting syndicate. Dryden Vos enjoys dressing up and hosting elaborate parties, but he's got the temper of a blurrg. He will not last long. When you reach the top, you need people you trust to have your back."
D00CF65464C7D64E0000E10E69F3546A,"A lot of inexperienced smugglers will ask me how to deal with bounty hunters, but the answer is very simple. Bounty hunters only care for credits, so unless you can outbid a crime lord, your best approach is to blast them and hope they didn't bring friends."
D00CF65464C7D65A0000E1128B47ADBE,"Being a successful smuggler depends on how you handle your cargo. You need a ship with secret compartments, and usually you will have to make them yourself. I'm proud to say that the Trailblazer is so good in this regard that even I can't find all of them anymore."
D00CF65464C7D6760000E11A9A63520A,"People who think Vandor is cold have clearly not visited Kijimi. Even with the thermal systems around the city, the planet is barely habitable unless you have a steady supply of soup and gristmeal tea."
D00CF65464C7D6840000E120E4D07C94,"If you ever have anything stolen, it is likely that it will eventually end up in the Thieves' District on Kijimi. I must admit that I have fenced a fair amount of goods here myself."
D00CF65464C7D6930000E1242031F212,"You cannot be in this trade without dealing with the Hutts. It is a fact of life. But you must make sure to stay on their good side. They have deep pockets, plenty of bounty hunters and a nasty sadistic streak."
D00CF65464C7D6A40000E128CD195891,"I like Chalmun's cantina. It has a rough and tumble feel, but you have to remember to keep one eye on the blaster and one eye on the exit. You never want to find yourself cornered in a basement."
D00CF65464C7D6F50000E132657E2493,"My father used to work for Jabba and kept telling me that Jabba never forgets. My father ended up getting dragged back to Tatooine for owing him a few thousand credits. As far as I know, he is still down there in the Sarlacc pit..."
D00CF65464C7D7020000E136F373E069,"Mos Eisley gets a bad reputation, for a good reason. Everyone is a scoundrel, including the Jawas, the droidsmiths and even the water merchants. If that bothers you, you're in the wrong line of work."
D00CF65464C7D7100000E13AD459E0F3,"I always wondered, out of all the places in Hutt Space, why Jabba set up shop on Tatooine. I think he just loves sitting in that palace, watching his subjects suffer in the desert."
D00CF65464C7D71C0000E13EBE8C964A,"Most people think the Tusken are all one and the same. That's a big mistake, as there are many different tribes with their own cultures and values. So don't go out there assuming you know anything, because you probably don't."
D00CF65464C7D7750000E14A8C9ABF7D,"The water tax... what kind of monster would tax farmers on the one thing that sustains life on this cruel, desert world? No one but Jabba would have that idea, even though it remains one of Tatooine's biggest mysteries what he uses it for."
D00CF65464C7D78A0000E14EE68D617A,"I was not surprised that the Clone Wars paved the way for the Empire. The galaxy was in pieces, and everyone wanted to be done with the war. I don't think they realized the price they paid. Maybe they never will."
D00CF65464C7D7970000E156AF538BA8,"The Kessel Run is a real test for a pilot. Some pilots want to use precaution and stay within the regular twenty parsec route, but most pilots who end up successful in this business will at least pass through the Corkscrew."
D00CF65464C7D7A80000E15A25FEB1B3,"The Pykes are an institution, and as long as you adapt to their ways you will find a moderate amount of success. Smugglers like us will always have a place in their plan. The key is to nod along and take the credits."
D00CF65464C7D7BF0000E15E6867DCED,"Many smugglers who pass through Toshara make the mistake that Mirogana is the center of commerce. Stay on Toshara long enough, you will realize that the diner in Jaunta's Hope is a much more interesting venue. The speakeasy downstairs has Imperials and criminals alike doing business, far away from the Pykes in Mirogana."
D00CF65464C7D7D00000E1621F45E8FA,"It is commonly thought that Canto Bight has the best Sabacc tables, but you should not underestimate Makal's in Mirogana. I recently partnered up with a Gallusian card counter named Bosnok, and together we made nearly ten thousand credits in one night. You will not see that type of action at the Daystar Casino."
D00CF65464C7D7DE0000E166E90E5344,"Mirogana has changed over the years, and every time I visit, it seems that the Empire is pulling back and the Pykes are taking over. But you must look beyond the streets and territories. As long as the Empire holds the spaceport, they are in charge."
D00CF65464C7D7ED0000E16A427A69A9,"There is no place quite like Toshara. You have the Pykes and the Empire side by side, and for a small cut you can get an Imperial certificate for almost anything. It is not always worth it, but sometimes you need to get goods off your hands."
D00CF65464C8D96900021A66DF6ADEE5,"Sixth Kin is a criminal organization based in Canto Bight's Worker's District. While considered small-time by galactic standards, Sixth Kin holds a lot of power in the Worker's District. Operating from the nightclub Club Tarsus, they make money by smuggling exotic animals, staging fights and races, and selling counterfeit luxury goods. While some avoid dealing with Sixth Kin due to their bad reputation, many have no choice but to give them their dues."
D00CF65464C8D96900021A675D9FB322,Sixth Kin
D00CF65464C8DDBF0002ACB8BC2F7D3C,"The Pykes are an old and wealthy syndicate that values tradition and status. Their spice mining operation on Kessel is further complemented with coaxium, smuggling and black-market distribution. The Pykes are spread out across the galaxy and are involved in every possible criminal enterprise. Their operation is incredibly well-funded, with starfighters, freighters, and advanced weaponry of every kind. They are a dangerous enemy and powerful ally."
D00CF65464C8DDBF0002ACB98EE843DF,Pyke Syndicate
D00CF65464C8DDC80002ACBF4BBFD4DA,"Zerek Besh is a new crime syndicate in the galactic underworld. Led by the wealthy Canto Bight socialite Sliro, the syndicate has had immense success undercutting the competition, disposing of enemies and establishing lucrative smuggling routes. With expertly trained enforcers, and suspiciously deep pockets, Zerek Besh is involved in a variety of illegal activities, such as smuggling, extortion and gambling."
D00CF65464C8DDC80002ACC096A7E4AA,Zerek Besh
D00CF65464C8DDCD0002ACC6E9BAA75D,"Crimson Dawn recently emerged from relative obscurity under the new leadership of Lady Qi'ra. Crimson Dawn is incredibly evasive, avoiding direct confrontation with rival syndicates in favor of political schemes, espionage, and assassinations. Everything that Crimson Dawn does serves a higher, secret agenda, with some believing that they have deliberately orchestrated a syndicate war between their rivals for their own ends."
D00CF65464C8DDCD0002ACC79865E9D0,Crimson Dawn
D00CF65464C8DDD20002ACCD5EDF7B33,"The Hutt Cartel is an ancient criminal organization with an abundance of wealth and power. While the cartel has traditionally been ruled by a council of Hutts, recent developments have led to Jabba Desilijic Tiure becoming the single-most powerful crime lord in the cartel. The Hutt Cartel is debauched and ruthless, relying on brute force and intimidation to seize power and defeat their enemies."
D00CF65464C8DDD20002ACCEA971CA59,Hutt Cartel
D00CF65464C8DDD70002ACD4A7DD8B5D,"The Ashiga Clan is a reclusive crime syndicate from Kijimi, centered around a hive of Melitto. Ruled by the singular authority of their Queen, the Ashiga act as a single, indivisible unit, which has helped them outlast many challenges in Kijimi's criminal underworld. However, following the Queen's decision to expand to other systems, and sell off resources to the Empire, the once intact hive is now suffering internal turmoil."
D00CF65464C8DDD70002ACD5CEDE4961,Ashiga Clan
D00CF65464C8DDDD0002ACDB9BC65F14,"The Galactic Empire was formed in the aftermath of the Clone Wars. Ruled from Coruscant under Emperor Palpatine, the Empire occupies most major systems in the galaxy, and is engaged in a violent civil war against a widespread rebellion. The Empire is terrible for business for outlaws, and they will go to great lengths to hunt down and punish criminals."
D00CF65464C8DDDD0002ACDCE1A9A566,Galactic Empire
D00CF65464C8DDE20002ACE25B615193,"The Rebel Alliance is a resistance movement engaged in a civil war against the Galactic Empire. Following a major win with the destruction of the Death Star, the rebels are now on the backfoot after a devastating defeat on Hoth. Now the rebel fleet is scattered and hidden, and rebel agents attempt to regroup to pick up the fight once again against the Empire."
D00CF65464C8DDE20002ACE325D9EEE5,Rebel Alliance
D4F6307964C8EF7C0003A03B55005438,Koje's Journal
D4F6307964C8EF9A0003A03E3932B325,"I'll just tell the Hutts I can't pay them. I'm sure they'll understand... Ha! I almost believed that for second.

Well here it is. Can't run forever. While I'm almost certainly a dead man, at least I won't have to put up with that annoying droid any longer."
DA5615DD64C8C0550000C13EC89CBF90,Miner
DA5615DD64C8C09E0000C143FFD8B4BF,Smuggler
