B4FBE43064D1E4E700006EEE8EA87871,CO-BA Countermeasures
D00CF65464CD1E350000C838FE3B714E,"Robumas are mammal herbivores that were domesticated when the first refugees landed on Toshara. They are herd animals by instinct, and wild herds of robumas can still be found roaming the savanna. Most Tosharan farmers will have them released in grazing territories as well, using speeders and droids to move them. Robumas are essential to Tosharan culture, with their milk, meat and leather commonly used in various ways."
D00CF65464CD1E350000C83987C3C851,Robuma
D00CF65464CD1F880000C8413CE433F0,"Ronga bugs are small insects with light-emitting organs that allow them to locate each other in darkness, and can mostly be found outside of Toshara's settlements. Ronga bugs are traditionally considered to bring good fortune if they land in someone's hand, and many Tosharan fairytales and folk stories revolve around receiving advice or wishes from magical ronga bugs."
D00CF65464CD1F880000C842DC318EC1,Ronga Bug
D00CF65464CD1F8D0000C848B79529EC,"Aglis flyers, or just flyers as they're often known colloquially by Tosharans, are winged creatures that are popular for their delicious meat. The aglis flyers are notorious for stealing anything they can get their hands on, hoarding belongings in remote nests. Even though they are both agile and have highly developed senses of sight, the Tosharan wind-fishing nets are very effective in capturing them."
D00CF65464CD1F8D0000C8493D2D5129,Aglis Flyer
D00CF65464CD1F910000C84F7C5CC2FC,"Yubesho rats are some of the most despised pests on Toshara, outnumbering sentient beings in Mirogana at least ten-fold. They are evasive, aggressive and will dig through dirt, wood and even metal with little effort to get a hold of food. While they are nearly blind due to living mostly underground, their heightened sense of smell lets them seek out food from great distances."
D00CF65464CD1F910000C850ADD50F45,Yubesho Rat
D00CF65464CD1F960000C856BB002FAA,"Gushiros are small and evasive mammals native to Toshara. They have long and slender bodies covered in dense fur. They mostly move around shrublands hunting for insects or smaller rodents, but they can also be seen in settlements, eating garbage or leftovers. Many cantina and restaurants have to have strict sanitation rules to ward off gushiros, as they are known to break into garbage containers."
D00CF65464CD1F960000C8573FEBEC99,Gushiro
D00CF65464CD1F9A0000C85D2CD52A5D,"Kama birds are large birds with wide wingspans that can be found around open savannas on Toshara. The birds are predatory and will actively seek out robuma calves as their preferred prey, circling around herds for long stretches of time before striking. Many robuma farmers will fire blasters at the mere sight of a kama bird, and even wild robumas have learned to keep their calves protected from aerial strikes."
D00CF65464CD1F9A0000C85E492167C8,Kama Bird
D00CF65464CD1FA40000C864A5E297EF,Apono moths are insects native to Toshara that have developed strong wings that allow them to stay airborne despite the moon's harsh winds. The aponos' wings are covered in vibrant and changing colors which they use to communicate with each other. Their fat bodies and tendency to stay at low altitudes have made them a primary target for gushiros.
D00CF65464CD1FA40000C8650E425064,Apono Moth
D00CF65464CD1FAC0000C86B62A40AB7,"The varaki are fierce predators native to Toshara that typically feed off smaller animals. Many Tosharan farmers have had to make special precautions to protect grazing robumas from varaki attacks. While this hard stance against varaki has reduced their population significantly, remaining varaki have adapted and become exceedingly clever. They have excellent senses of smell, and their hardened tails can release sharp quills when threatened."
D00CF65464CD1FAC0000C86C888F320B,Varaki
D00CF65464CD20910000C879D2E353E9,"Banthas are large, hairy mammals with spiraling horns that are often used as domesticated herd animals. Banthas are omnivores and can sustain energy without food or water for long stretches of time. Many farmers use banthas for their milk, meat and leather."
D00CF65464CD20910000C87A916310C9,Bantha
D00CF65464CD210C0000C88137C60248,"Dewbacks are large thick-skinned reptiles that are native to Tatooine. Their ability to be trained and domesticated, as well as their innate resilience and durability, have led to them being used as mounts by both locals on Tatooine as well as Imperial troopers."
D00CF65464CD210C0000C882CB74989A,Dewback
D00CF65464CD212B0000C88876A3D9CD,"Dust rats are common rats that can be found across all of Tatooine's settlements. Relying entirely off leftovers and trash from people, the dust rats are widely considered pests that can severely damage farms and houses."
D00CF65464CD212B0000C889466789FC,Dust Rat
D00CF65464CD214B0000C89192EDE926,"Skettos are nocturnal blood-sucking flying reptiles that can be found in caverns on Tatooine. While they mostly feed off smaller insects, they are also known for latching onto larger creatures, like banthas and dewbacks, extracting nutritious blood from them overnight."
D00CF65464CD214B0000C892CE3DAA3A,Sketto
D00CF65464CD21830000C89892BC1EAF,"Krayt dragons are massive serpent-like creatures that roam around the desert of Tatooine. While they are known for occasionally attacking settlements, they are primarily a threat to travelers out in the sand dunes."
D00CF65464CD21830000C8990D5008AF,Krayt Dragon
D00CF65464CD219A0000C89FD1FCBDF0,"Flyhorn lizards are solitary creatures that live out in the desert, using their tails and horns to catch condensation and smaller insects while staying cool in the sand. Some moisture farmers have a habit of observing flyhorns near their farms to evaluate their yields."
D00CF65464CD219A0000C8A0D48B5D32,Flyhorn Lizard
D00CF65464CD21B50000C8A604EF8F91,"Bonegnawers are large birds of prey native to Tatooine with strong beaks that can crush rocks and bones. They are known for stalking relatively large prey and consuming them on the spot, taking the bones back to their nests to feed off the marrow and share it with their young."
D00CF65464CD21B50000C8A7558EF024,Bonegnawer
D00CF65464CD21E20000C8B14AC68B68,"Nobaki rats are small rat-like creatures that can be found everywhere in Kijimi City. Like rats on many other worlds, the nobaki live off whatever trash and leftovers people leave behind, and they are considered a pest. The nobaki are still very popular among children, which has led to some people keeping tame nobaki as pets."
D00CF65464CD21E20000C8B27A9E2D83,Nobaki Rat
D00CF65464CD22190000C8C0944E7B9B,"Henku are large warm-blooded mammals with thick skins and fur that make them ideal cattle for cold worlds like Kijimi. The henku are believed to share a common ancestry with banthas, and they are also used for their milk, meat and leather. Fishers on Kijimi will often use henku as beasts of burden to transport goods between lakes and settlements."
D00CF65464CD22190000C8C1CACA35F8,Henku
D00CF65464CD222D0000C8C75F7A9347,"Kyumo rabbits are small mammals that are resilient survivors in the harsh climate on Kijimi. The kyumos' sensitive ears, long nose and high agility make them fully aware of threats in their surroundings, and they will either run or dig into the snow to hide."
D00CF65464CD222D0000C8C8FBA59A73,Kyumo Rabbit
D00CF65464CD22420000C8CE1C89FD44,"Valaracs are nomadic birds with exceptional vision that allows them to hunt prey at great distances. Their wing serrations allow them to fly quietly, making them virtually silent right before striking at prey. While valaracs will often move around Kijimi in search of warmer climates, they can often be found around thermal wells while migrating."
D00CF65464CD22420000C8CFE02B1896,Valarac
D00CF65464CD225E0000C8D5C1459E19,"Venga are amphibians on Akiva that can mostly be found in the wetlands, even though they will migrate to other areas in search for food, particularly during rain seasons. They are opportunistic predators who will stalk and ambush their prey, and their enhanced senses can make light of almost any type of natural camouflage."
D00CF65464CD225E0000C8D69B619E2B,Venga
D00CF65464CD22B20000C8E05E53398B,"Sommato birds are freshwater birds that live near large bodies of water. Their skin is covered in scales and they have large webbings on their feet, which makes the sommato birds excellent swimmers and divers."
D00CF65464CD22B20000C8E1FB8F4FA4,Sommato Bird
D00CF65464CD22E90000C8E79FFD16CA,"Shaparaks are robust insects with expressive patterns on their wings to scare away predators. The shaparaks are docile and intelligent, and they will emit pacifying waves with their wings to subdue potential threats. Many Akivans believe watching wild shaparaks can have a soothing effect on anxious minds."
D00CF65464CD22E90000C8E84CC0BD05,Shaparak
D00CF65464CD22FD0000C8EEFFF7BEB6,"Originally stemming from Kowak, the Akivan monkey-lizards are assumed to have been accidentally introduced to the Akivan ecosystem by a careless traveler. The monkey-lizards'  ability to live off of almost any type of sustenance caused their population to explode, where many of them actively seek out settlements and travelers in the jungle to steal food and valuables off them."
D00CF65464CD22FD0000C8EF4E8E6A70,Monkey Lizard
D00CF65464CD231B0000C8F5D15F6402,"Jabarek lizards can be found across all of Akiva, even though they tend to prefer living around lakes and larger bodies of water. The jabarek are excellent swimmers and have two sets of eyes, one of which is especially adapted to spotting fish deep under the surface."
D00CF65464CD231B0000C8F6E49A984F,Jabarek Lizard
D00CF65464CD23330000C8FC9E6F1E62,"Ya-ya flies can be found everywhere on Akiva. While they don't present a threat to most organic beings, their numbers have earned them a reputation of being one of the worst annoyances about Akiva. Ya-ya flies will arrive in large numbers after rain seasons, which has led to some people catching them as a source of food."
D00CF65464CD23330000C8FD3BF26B2A,Ya-Ya Fly
D00CF65464D0F09D0002C4C728FE2F31,Toshara's wildlife is diverse but has all evolved to thrive in the moon's windy atmosphere and warm climate.
D00CF65464D0F09D0002C4C89454918D,Fauna
D00CF65464D0F8DD0002C4DF80A37836,Tatooine's hot and dry climate puts immense pressure on all life but has still managed to sustain a variety of different species.
D00CF65464D0F8DD0002C4E06EC5A6EF,Fauna
D00CF65464D0F9160002C4EE83DBF5EB,Kijimi's low temperature and lack of sunlight has paved the way for some resilient creatures that can still survive and thrive in the planet's harsh climate.
D00CF65464D0F9160002C4EF696CDE82,Fauna
D00CF65464D0F9DD0002C4FA94B1489B,Akiva contains a vibrant and unique ecosystem and its wildlife thrives in the planet's lush and wet jungles.
D00CF65464D0F9DD0002C4FB448AA619,Fauna
D00CF65464D0FB3A0000C8728FD3CA0F,"Akiva is a hot and humid planet in the Outer Rim Territories, famous for its heavy rainstorms. While the planet is under Imperial control, they rule it indirectly via the Akivan satrapy and only visit during the decennial tax audits. Because of the Empire's general absence, and the planet's history of separatist droid production, Akiva is festered with corruption and a thriving black market."
D00CF65464D0FB3A0000C873F112404A,Akiva
D00CF65464D1069900016DFEAB30EB1A,Extra Refund
