BE6ABC7665339BD800020D715DF322EB,Plant the spike
CC69B221653153D100017FFA6198B35E,Speeder Remote
CC69B221653153D100017FFBA74A786A,"A small device that sends a control signal to the speeder, which  uses real-time telemetry data to travel automatically to its owner."
CC69B221653153D100017FFC2D5559EB,A device used to call the Speeder from anywhere.
CC69B22165364BA800008F0C1C50E6B4,Fusioncutter
CC69B22165364BA800008F0D6636C777, A handheld device equipped with an energy cell to create a high temperature plasma arc to melt metal and various other materials.
CC69B22165364BA800008F0E517AFD8E,Used to cut through weak metal to open a path.
D00CF6546531505A00016CE6024632A4,"MT-7 is a BX Commando droid from the Clone Wars. But unlike ND-5, he never saw much action. His very first mission was to travel to Akiva with a squad of B1 Droids and find the crashed ship of a high-ranking Separatist officer. But disaster struck almost immediately: He was severely damaged in one of the planet's legendary torrential downpours and separated from the rest of his crew."
D00CF6546531505A00016CE7C97AC1F8,MT-7
D00CF65465323ECA0001247874F96FE8,ISB Report : Bram Shano
D00CF65465323F390001247AE4B1F8D3,"NAME: Bram Shano
AGE: 48
OCCUPATION: Bar owner

Bram is the owner and proprietor of The Broken Hoof, a popular sports bar in Canto Bight's Worker's District. Investigations into his affairs indicate that he's running a legitimate business but there are unverified rumors that he's involved with brokering robberies, bookkeeping rigged fights and races, and operating as a fence for stolen goods. 

These appear to be small-scale activities, and the ISB's primary concern in Canto Bight should instead be Wen Delphis and the Sixth Kin gang, which Bram is completely unaffiliated with."
D00CF65465323F9E0001247B7EDBA630,"NAME: Sliro Ruback
AGE: Unknown
OCCUPATION: Syndicate leader

Sliro is a crime lord and the leader of the Zerek Besh crime syndicate, operating from Westhill Palace in Canto Bight. Investigations into Sliro's past reveal that he comes from the social elite on Alderaan and that a sizable part of his fortune was made from fraudulent investments following the destruction of the planet. 

Sliro has been running investment schemes and extortion rackets in Canto Bight for years, taking the Zerek Besh crime organization from a local Canto Bight entity to a galaxy-wide crime syndicate.

Sliro recently had several representatives from rival syndicates invited over to Westhill Palace and had them killed to send a threatening message to their superiors. The ISB's monitoring of the criminal underworld has shown that it's been effective, and that several syndicates are actively looking to retaliate."
D00CF65465323F9F0001247CC1E2002C,ISB Report : Sliro Ruback
D00CF65465323FF90001247FD19DA060,ISB Report : Ank Parako
D00CF65465323FFB000124828B9CCE95,"NAME: Ank Parako
AGE: 40
OCCUPATION: Safecracker

Ank has a considerable criminal record of robberies and other felonies, most of them perpetrated together with her now deceased husband Pirrip. With a criminal career spanning over twenty years, Ank and Pirrip were responsible for damages of over 590 million credits and were remarkably never arrested or detained. 

Thankfully, Ank's irresponsible behavior appears to have caused the end of her own career, as a botched vault robbery on Kijimi led to her capture at the hands of the Ashiga Clan. Investigations into this have revealed that Ank is working off her debts in the clan's weapons factory. Considering Ank's relatively old age for a Chadra-fan, it is unlikely that she will ever be released."
D00CF6546532401E00012485D4A58563,ISB Report : Asara Deyn
D00CF6546532401F000124883533FE4B,"NAME: Asara Deyn
AGE: 18
OCCUPATION: Rebel spy

Asara Deyn is a verified member of the Rebel Alliance who should be considered a class 2 threat to the Galactic Empire. The ISB's investigations into Asara suggest that he grew up on Akiva with his parents and his sister Calys. Calys organized a local insurgency, and she managed to recruit Asara after making contact with a field agent from the Rebel Alliance. 

Calys left Akiva shortly after that and was killed months later in the Battle of Scarif. The ISB has information that suggests it was a tipping point for Asara, causing him to reach out to the rebel handler and join the rebellion in an official capacity. 

Evaluations of Asara's psychological profile suggest that the trauma of his sister is a strong pressure point that can be exploited upon his capture, and that it's likely that he will have access to actionable intelligence at any given time."
D00CF654653240330001248B32436C8B,ISB Report : Gedeek Obaz
D00CF654653240340001248EAD086C84,"NAME: Gedeek Obaz
AGE: 23
OCCUPATION: Droidsmith

Gedeek is a Rodian droidsmith from Canto Bight who has recently been taken into employment by the Imperial Engineering Corps on Akiva. Investigations into Gedeek's past suggest a handful of small transgressions that were considered low risk at the time of his hiring. 

Further surveillance of his time on Akiva, however, suggests that he's been involved in assembling droids for underground cage fights, receiving payment from both the Pyke Syndicate and the Hutt Cartel. In the future, it could be pertinent to use Gedeek as an informant to infiltrate these activities."
D00CF65465324043000124919D0B30B9,ISB Report : Hoss
D00CF654653240440001249462675E4B,"NAME: Hoss
AGE: 63
OCCUPATION: Mercenary

Hoss has a longstanding reputation as one of the fiercest mercenaries in the galaxy, earning him a death sentence on six systems. Despite his involvement in numerous felonies, including fraud, larceny, burglary and more counts of murder than is reasonable to list, Hoss has never managed to sustain any fruitful collaborations with any of the major crime syndicates. 

All investigations so far into Hoss' criminal career points to him being widely considered a volatile liability, and it's reasonable to believe that he will eventually cause his own demise – whether it's from the countless debts he owes to the galaxy's most powerful crime lords, or from getting betrayed by temporary partners that see him as a risk."
D00CF65465324052000124973E629A0C,ISB Report : ND-5
D00CF654653240530001249A3D5C0F53,"NAME: ND-5
AGE: 25
OCCUPATION: Enforcer

ND-5 is a BX Commando droid who was marked for decommission following a failed operation during the Clone Wars, but somehow ended up on the black market. Shortly after the end of the Clone Wars, ND-5 came into possession of crime lord Jaylen Vrax who has been using the droid as his personal bodyguard and enforcer for several years. 

ND-5 has been identified as involved in numerous incidents all over the galaxy. ND-5 is recognizable by extensive damage on the chassis, some of which is covered up by the droid's odd use of a trench coat."
D00CF654653240630001249DD877107E,ISB Report : Danka Orsato
D00CF65465324063000124A03682A63E,"NAME: Danka Orsato
AGE: Unknown
OCCUPATION: Information broker
Danka Orsato is an information broker on Toshara with a wide network of contacts within various criminal organizations. While Danka has been both directly and indirectly involved in major felonies, both on Toshara and in other systems, she has willingly collaborated with the ISB and supplied us with actionable information that has led to the capture of several high-profile individuals. 

Danka is a valuable figure on Toshara and should be considered an asset that can be used to great effect, albeit in a limited capacity. She must stay a believably neutral party to remain effective, which means the ISB must allow certain transgressions to happen."
D00CF65465324075000124A3ECF96174,ISB Report : Eleera Soi
D00CF65465324076000124A665B1DEAC,"NAME: Eleera Soi
AGE: 38
OCCUPATION: Syndicate agent

The ISB's investigation indicates that Eleera is part of Crimson Dawn's inner circle with a history going back to the leader Qi'ra's early days in the syndicate. She is mostly operating on her own as a field agent and handler. Her main responsibility is to compromise the Pyke Syndicate, focusing primarily on their foothold on Toshara. Due to her direct involvement with Qi'ra, Eleera should be considered a class 2 threat to the Galactic Empire."
D00CF6546532408A000124A915A0B2B2,ISB Report : Gorak Palas
D00CF6546532408B000124AC4CF95EA7,"NAME: Gorak Palas
AGE: 47
OCCUPATION: Crime lord

Gorak is the Pyke Syndicate's main representative on Toshara who has established the Pykes as the most powerful crime syndicate in the system. Gorak has set up a vast network of contacts and allies on Toshara, with many of them being high-ranking officers within the Imperial Sector Command. 

Upon queries, Imperial Governor Thorden claims that the Pyke Syndicate's dominant position has had a stabilizing effect on the criminal elements of the system and that they are under close surveillance. The ISB will continue to monitor both Gorak's and Governor Thorden's activities with several deployed loyalty officers operating under cover."
D00CF6546532409E000124AF5EAD7493,ISB Report : Jabba Desilijic Tiure
D00CF6546532409F000124B28156BCB8,"NAME: Jabba Desiljic Tiure
AGE: Unknown
OCCUPATION: Syndicate leader

Jabba Desilijic Tiure is one of the most powerful and long-standing crime lords in the galaxy and currently the only surviving member of the Hutt Council, leaving him in complete control of the Hutt Cartel. Due to the vastness of his recorded crimes and the ongoing investigations surrounding Jabba, all cases are being handled by a special investigation group within the ISB. 

While the group is prohibited from making an official criminal charge against Jabba until clearance from the highest level, the case files are often referenced and utilized when charging the cartel's affiliates."
D00CF654653240AD000124B5349885EE,ISB Report : Jaylen Vrax
D00CF654653240AE000124B8BD4832CE,"NAME: Jaylen Vrax
AGE: Unknown
OCCUPATION: Crime lord

Jaylen Vrax is an independent crime lord and gunrunner from Coruscant's underworld level 1523 with a significant criminal record, including fraud, forgery, smuggling and extortion. 

While Jaylen is unaffiliated with any known crime syndicates, the ISB's investigations suggest sporadic involvement with some of the galaxy's major crime syndicates although no formal alliances or partnerships appear to have been established. 

The ISB's investigations into Jaylen's activities suggest that he maintains a light and mobile operation, relying mostly on freelancers as well as his personal bodyguard and enforcer, a BX Commando droid called ND-5. All things considered; Jaylen does not pose a significant threat to galactic security."
D00CF654653240BF000124BBB314E19F,ISB Report : Qi'ra
D00CF654653240C0000124BEB2F7463A,"NAME: Qi'ra
AGE: Unknown
OCCUPATION: Possible syndicate leader

Qi'ra is the suspected leader of the Crimson Dawn crime syndicate and should be considered a class 1 threat against Imperial interests. Through the ISB's investigation, it's highly likely that the recent syndicate war is the result of an operation orchestrated by Qi'ra and Crimson Dawn. 

The report suggests that Qi'ra convinced several major crime syndicates that the Empire is ending an arrangement with the Hutt Cartel and will grant special privileges to a competitor.

Furthermore, Qi'ra is believed to have been involved in several other incidents with varying degrees of evidence, including the assassination of the Emperor's Royal Guard and a raid on Mustafar. Regardless of her involvement, Qi'ra poses a serious threat to the galactic order and the sovereignty of the Galactic Empire."
D00CF654653240D7000124C1850ACE3F,ISB Report : Queen Ashiga
D00CF654653240D8000124C4FDF7300C,"NAME: Queen Ashiga
AGE: Unknown
OCCUPATION: Syndicate leader

Queen Ashiga is the leader of the Ashiga Clan crime syndicate that was established on Kijimi during the High Republic. Investigations into their leadership structure suggest that the individual known as the Queen is just one of many in a series of successions, making it difficult to verify her identity and age.

Unlike most criminal syndicates, the Ashiga Clan has remained isolated on Kijimi for the greater part of their history, but new information suggests that the Queen is looking to expand their territories to other systems. 

This, along with the Empire's trade with the Ashiga Clan, has led to internal friction, which we believe may cause a collapse within the syndicate. It is suggested that the Empire should stand down and let this happen, as it will open new opportunities on Kijimi."
D00CF654653240E7000124C7134AA37F,ISB Report : Surat Nuat
D00CF654653240E8000124CA1B5E6188,"NAME: Surat Nuat
AGE: Unknown
OCCUPATION: Crime lord

Surat Nuat is the leader of a local gang on Akiva with minimal activity outside of the local system. As the owner and proprietor of the popular cantina The Alcazar in the capital Myrra, Surat generates immense profits, especially from gambling. 

Recent investigations into Surat's affairs point to him having established a collaboration with Jabba and the Hutt Cartel, paying tribute to Jabba in exchange for weapons and hired hands. 

While this can imply that the Hutts are looking to establish a bigger presence on Akiva, our ISB analysts believe that the alliance is fragile and will likely dissolve in the near future. For now, Surat and his support from the Hutt Cartel are proving useful in tempering the increased threat of the Pyke Syndicate, and it's recommended that he is left alone."
D00CF654653240FA000124CD772BB9D9,ISB Report : Sliro Ruback
D00CF654653240FC000124D080EF995D,"NAME: Sliro Ruback
AGE: Unknown
OCCUPATION: Syndicate leader

Sliro is a crime lord and the leader of the Zerek Besh crime syndicate, operating from Westhill Palace in Canto Bight. Investigations into Sliro's past reveal that he comes from the social elite on Alderaan and that a sizable part of his fortune was made from fraudulent investments following the destruction of the planet. 

Sliro has been running investment schemes and extortion rackets in Canto Bight for years, taking the Zerek Besh crime organization from a local Canto Bight entity to a galaxy-wide crime syndicate.

Sliro recently had several representatives from rival syndicates invited over to Westhill Palace and had them killed to send a threatening message to their superiors. The ISB's monitoring of the criminal underworld has shown that it's been effective, and that several syndicates are actively looking to retaliate."
D00CF65465324105000124D3768601DD,ISB Report : Vail Tormin
D00CF65465324106000124D6BDA9ABF4,"NAME: Vail Tormin
AGE: 25
OCCUPATION: Bounty hunter

Vail is a bounty hunter with an impressive track record considering her young age, earning her a reputation as one of the best the bounty hunter guild has to offer. Vail notably assassinated the crime lord Slem Slonini which led to the collapse of the Slonini Cartel, increasing Vail's value by almost 350%.

Achievements aside, Vail has shown a hard stance against taking on Imperial bounties, which has the ISB investigating possible affiliations with rebels or anti-Imperial activists. So far, no such affiliations have been identified. It's possible that some personal experience has made her reluctant to collaborate with the Empire without making her an active insurgent. Nevertheless, Vail's work with prominent syndicates, such as Black Sun and Zerek Besh will often put her at odds with Imperial interests."
D00CF65465324117000124D97D9BDAE6,ISB Report : Riko Vess
D00CF65465324118000124DC4BFDAC27,"NAME: Riko Vess
AGE: 50
OCCUPATION: Slicer and thief

Riko Vess has an extensive criminal record and has worked with several criminal organizations throughout her career as a slicer and a thief. Riko was believed to have retired shortly after the Clone Wars, but the ISB's investigations have revealed that she was living in Canto Bight with her daughter, Kay Vess. 

Riko is suspected of having been involved in numerous thefts and burglaries during that time, but she eventually left Canto Bight and her daughter and became more directly involved with the major crime syndicates in the Outer Rim.

Over the years, Riko has built up a reputation of being one of the most skilled slicers in the underworld, having infiltrated some of the galaxy's most secure networks, including the Imperial Galactic Bank and the Imperial Court. While Riko does not appear to be affiliated with the Rebel Alliance, it is reasonable to think that she could cause significant harm to the Empire if given sufficient motivation. As such, the ISB is considering Riko Vess a class 2 threat."
D00CF65465324128000124DF62947300,ISB Report : Kay Vess
D00CF65465324129000124E2457D1702,"NAME: Kay Vess 
AGE: 22
OCCUPATION: Thief 

Kay Vess was reported to the ISB after stealing a private starship belonging to crime lord Sliro of the Zerek Besh crime syndicate. Further investigations revealed that Vess has lived in Canto Bight her whole life and has had several run-ins with Canto Bight police, mainly regarding theft and burglary.  

While some of the other suspects in the Westhill Palace robbery are known members of the Rebel Alliance, it is unlikely that Kay Vess is an active member herself. Her mother Riko Vess is unaffiliated with the rebels, and Kay Vess has not been in contact with anyone on the ISB Canto Bight watchlist. 

However, the risk of her being recruited in the future is significant and she must be considered a threat to the Galactic Empire."
