C7AA9ADA65367FC7004F3EC1EED32934,"The legendary slicer Aila Bren has some advanced tech that Kay could use, but it won’t come free. First, Kay has to do Aila a favor."
D4F6307965365F5C001C345C83FADC0D,Day 1
D4F6307965365F5C001C345D9E6A79E7,"So here I am, making my own opportunities. They call this place Tatooine. Our benefactor is convinced this miserable dust bowl harbors phrik worth millions. Whoever they are, I hope they’re right.

Everyone in camp has a story, but something tells me I’m not the only one with a bounty on my head. I can see it on their faces – everyone’s hiding something. We get along fine, but I won’t pretend to truly know them, let alone call them friends.

It is what it is, a ragtag group of criminals looking to change their fortunes."
D4F6307965366161000108DDDA889B17,Day 92
D4F6307965366161000108DEEF1D3282,"Almost three months of toil, digging, loading, building, blasting rock, cutting paths, choking on sand, and for what? A fistful of phrik… That glimmer of hope we shared when we got here is already fading. Supply ships becoming increasingly sparse, rations are running low, and we’ve already lost half our crew.

Our benefactor’s growing impatient, demanding results. I’m starting to worry there’s nothing here."
D4F6307965366169000108E0C07725D0,Day 140
D4F6307965366169000108E15EB94EEA,"It’s just me now. The last of the crew left yesterday when our supply ship didn’t show up. I guess that means our benefactor has suspended operations.

It’s too bad I’ll have to leave all this equipment behind, but I’d rather spend the rest of my days in a penal colony than sleep another night in this place. Heard there’s a town beyond the Dune Sea. Perhaps I could hand myself in, tell whoever’ll listen who I really am."
