ACAEF5AB678F55D50004853C757F415D,The Final Rest p. 75
ACAEF5AB678F55D50004853DB8FC7B8C,"The simple truth is that there was no crisis to manage. No mass exodus of Khepi seeking shelter. In fact, when the news eventually reached the Khepi envoys on Coruscant, they all returned home. Elder A'shora reflected: ""We stand together and our faith in the Light is absolute. The Great Tomb will be completed as planned.""

Ye-Gimu, Lento. The Final Rest. 7918."
ACAEF5AB678F55F30004853F33B2383B,History of the Khepi p. 152
ACAEF5AB678F55F300048540183D678D,"It is difficult to grasp the scope of the Great Tomb since we have yet to find any concrete records of its construction. However, High Priestess O'lona stated in a message to the clergy that ""it is imperative that everyone is invited into the fold. Our very essence depends on it."" The logistics of achieving that in such a short time is truly a testament of the Khepi's dedication to the Final Ritual.

San Tekka, Lor. History of the Khepi. 7957."
ACAEF5AB678F55FC00048542BCB4A0F9,The Lost Tomb p. 190
ACAEF5AB678F55FC0004854355DD7898,"The choice of the Sayma Nebula as their final resting place was not arbitrary. As Lento Ye-Gimu explains, ""a central tenet in the Khepi faith was to send their deceased to the stars."" So, faced with impending doom, the clergy understood what their next chapter involved. As the Sayma Nebula would eventually collapse into a star, so too would the Khepi become one with the Light.

Graf, Rhyssa. The Lost Tomb. 7945."
ACAEF5AB678F56030004854501FBB2CA,Khepi Chronicles p. 38
ACAEF5AB678F5603000485460A497FF5,"While the Khepi were in regular contact with the High Republic and the Jedi Order, they declined their invitations to Coruscant on several occasions. High Priestess O'lona wrote in her journals after one such invitation that ""the Jedi have shown a great interest in our faith and organization. Their only mistake is thinking the interest is mutual.""

Jopeem, Molo. Khepi Chronicles. 7963"
ACAEF5AB678F560A000485488D780B7E,Secrets of the Khepi p. 340
ACAEF5AB678F560A0004854990A25A25,"The question is not whether or not the Khepi built the tomb. Everything points to this being factually true, even if it was not fully completed. No, the question is what measures the Khepi took to keep it safe until the nebula collapsed into a star. The Khepi were magnificent engineers and craftspeople, with advanced relics still being discovered across the galaxy. So what did they do to protect the tomb?

Charoo, Suna. Secrets of the Khepi. 7932."
