91D5D542679CDBE10000004645C23A73,The Rokana Code
91D5D542679CDBE1000000470120A4D9,"The crew votes on everything, and any raider can call for a vote. When a decision's made, everyone falls in line.

The crew chooses the captain. If the crew votes to replace the captain, the captain has to go.

Pay comes out of the haul from the raids. No prey, no pay.

The captain gets an equal share. Old timers get two shares. If a raider takes a bad hit or loses a limb, they get a share and a half.

Droids can't vote, and droids don't get shares.

The crew is loyal to each other. Not to other bands, not to the syndicates, and not to the government.

Any raider who shirks their watch or lets their blaster go rusty loses their share.

Any raider caught stealing or selling out the crew gets marooned on an asteroid with a day of air."
91D5D542679CDF840000004CA7FF5947,The Rokana Code (Annotated)
91D5D542679CDF840000004DEF76E48D,"Welcome aboard, newcomer. You're a Rokana raider now, and you take what you want! You had to recite the rules before you got that shiny new blaster, but let's make sure you actually understood them:

Stinger's the captain. You do whatever she says, whenever she says it, no matter the reason. You want to call for a vote, it's your head.

You get what Stinger says you get. Complain if you like, but you'll just end up with nothing.

Oh, and droids are machines. Don't get attached and don't treat 'em like people."
91D5D542679CE37100000058D5640B32,Punishments
91D5D542679CE371000000590CC2C71F,"Offense: Gar Tharik was caught pinching a bottle of rotgut from the supply rooms.
Sentence: No shares for the next five raids.
Ruled by: Crew vote

Offense: Paias Reef and Shifty Lin Vane tried to keep a stash of treasure secret from the crew.
Sentence: Thrown out the airlock. 
Ruled by: Stinger Tash

Offense: Big-Hands Leduu slept through the start of their shift.
Sentence: Standing first watch every day for the next month.
Ruled by: Crew vote

Offense: Orr Dayfinder badmouthed the captain and went against the Khepi plan after the whole crew voted on it.
Sentence: Marooned on abandoned space station Iris-5465.
Ruled by: Stinger Tash"
91D5D542679CE4FB00000064960F7FDC,Raider's Journal
91D5D542679CE4FB0000006534DBC70D,"Centaxday: Scouted a range at the far edge of the nebula but the ion storms keep pushing us back. Came back with an empty hold.

Taungsday: Got close to a debris cluster out by our search zone. Some alloys, a few mineral compounds, but nothing worth the time.

Zhellday: The ion storms cleared for a moment. We were able to pinpoint some roxodium units before it all clouded over again.

Benduday: Stashed the haul on the ledge near Trapper’s Gully. It was quite a climb, but at least it’ll be safe."
91D5D542679CE7EE000000706AE78E31,Expedition Journal
91D5D542679CE7EE00000071A3E3F1DC,"Journal of Professor Gil Orum, Imperial Science Academy

Khepi Expedition, day ten. On the surface, the Sayma Nebula is a standard Type 15A stellological phenomenon, similar to the Maelstrom Nebula or any of the larger formations in the Trax sector. But the mysteries beneath are unlike anything I've seen in all my years of surveying.

After employing the locals to rig up some improvised magnetoshields, we were able to penetrate the outer layer with our nav systems intact. What we saw beneath the clouds was thoroughly unexpected: another ship, drifting through space and unresponsive to our communications. When we approached, anxious the safety of whatever crew was aboard, it suddenly vanished. I might have questioned my sanity, had not all of us witnessed the same thing.

The Khepi system has fierce defenses of a nature I cannot quite determine. It puts me in mind of a sentient creature slashing at the interloper that dared to enter its lair. I try to keep a rational mind, but I cannot help the ominous feeling of trespassing. Of going somewhere I am not welcome.

In any case, it will make for a thrilling holomonograph."
