58006D5067A9CED7000000E704F425E6,Preempt pirate raid
58006D5067A9CEE9000000EC3131FF9C,Locate and raid the cargo ship
58006D5067A9CEF2000000EF45CB654F,"The client wants a daring pilot to learn the details of an upcoming pirate raid, then steal from their target before they get the chance. The pirates will probably come for their prize once they realize it's been stolen out from under their noses."
58006D5067A9D6B60000010267294F84,Steal cargo
58006D5067A9D6B600000103F08CFE5F,Locate and raid pirate ships
58006D5067A9D7010000010970E2E933,"The client needs a discreet but capable smuggler to acquire some sensitive cargo from a group of known pirates, then bring it to the drop point in Kijimi space."
9128788867A9B4B2000441760298311C,Quit Your Whining
9128788867A9B4B200044177243FDAD5,"Listen here, you sorry sack of sunflare skimmers! I been hearing too much jabbering and tendril-flapping out on the deck. 

The next time Ace Sunspinner starts complaining about Stinger being a bad captain, you shut it down and get back to work. Just because he keeps saying it doesn't mean you have to go along with it. 

I don't want my landing bay infested with do-nothings and mutineers. We clear?

Deckmaster Offo"
9128788867A9B4B200044178B5AEA10A,Who's On Story Detail?
9128788867A9B4B2000441790D122DC8,Ibess is on one again. Someone better come up with some good stories to tide him over. I don't want another mug of squelt tossed at my head in the tavern!
91D5D54267A5FF09000000E068E5180E,Gwarm's Orders
91D5D54267A5FF09000000E1D39F7AF0,"Put aside two spice crates from yesterday's raid. Don't add them to the inventory. Gwarm has a deal to follow up on.

Keep Hondo out of it... if that wasn't clear."
91D5D54267A5FFB3000000E60F0A7AC7,Wild Beasts
91D5D54267A5FFB3000000E7E2A83957,"The massiffs feed themselves by hunting in the canyon. Just keep out of their way if you value your limbs.

That pale creature with the hairy back is Hondo's new trophy pet. Make sure it's healthy and inside its enclosure. Two servings of meat a day.

Don't mess this up. I'll take over again when I'm back from this job."
91D5D54267A60015000000EC8FC42D51,Astromech
91D5D54267A60015000000EDFC5282F7,"DO NOT send R5-P8 out on any more errands. This was the third time he's almost been captured by Jawas. 
I know he desperately wants to be useful, but find him tasks inside the hideout instead."
91D5D54267A60128000000FDA95380DD,"Hondo's Memoirs, First Draft Excerpt"
91D5D54267A60128000000FEEED1C5B6,"Chapter 112. As I sit here in my luxurious desert hideout and think back on the many wonderful things that I have accomplished and stolen in my lifetime, I find that I am most grateful for the little things.

For example, I am grateful that I am such a cunning genius. It is a small blessing, but a real one. Many in my line of work lack the cool wit and resourcefulness which I demonstrated when I laid waste to the notorious Humbarine Ore Caravan, despite being outnumbered 30-to-1. I profited where my lesser rivals did not.

For that matter, few are ferocious or relentless as me. Lesser captains would shrink like wilting derrandelles when confronted with the fearsome Two-Headed Toothvole of Bogmadada. Not I. I steeled my courage and shot the creature right between its eyes. Then right between its other eyes! Ah, but perhaps that is a tale for a future chapter.

Yes, it is truly humbling to realize how much of one's success comes from the inherent heroic qualities that one is born with. I guess I can thank my dear mother for that. In fact... hmm. Note to self: let's circle back around to mother. I think she deserves a few more chapters. End dictation."
91D5D54267AA2582000000CEBD21D010,I Hate This Station
91D5D54267AA2582000000CFD57411CD,"Hauler’s Keep used to be a respectable station for us miners. Sure, it was never pretty, but you’d get a fair price for ore and could rent a class two berth without getting blasted in the back. Now you can’t do anything without the Trade League taking a cut, and they don’t lift a finger to protect you from pirates. The Mining Guild pulled out cycles ago. Maybe we should have gone too."
91D5D54267AA25EE000000D4209A2935,Our Future
91D5D54267AA25EE000000D5D2C4C84C,"The League must expand. To restore our power to the heights it reached during the Republic, we need to recruit independent smugglers. Yes, they’ll never know what it was like to solo the Miyuki Gap with Vectors on your tail, but we’re still a collective and we watch each other’s backs. The Bounty Hunter’s Guild made it work, now it’s our time."
91D5D54267AA270F000000DA2F846032,I Can't Protect You
91D5D54267AA270F000000DB5560F688,"You broke one rule, but it was the only rule that counts here. Rip off a syndicate? That’s between you and their enforcers. Blast a pirate? They’re always blasting each other anyways. You chose to interfere with the operations of the Miyuki Trade League on Hauler’s Keep, and now they’ve revoked your access to docking rights, ship fuel, and breathable air."
91D5D54267AA278B000000E0FC6FE026,To: IAD<br>From: Dr. Jessik
91D5D54267AA278B000000E19AAB4CA2,"We have it all wrong! The Khepi theocracy wasn’t obsessed with death, but with life itself. They saw the destruction of their planet at the height of the Republic not as an end, but as a beginning. The asteroid isn’t a tomb – it’s a cocoon. It’s like the whole species is gestating, waiting for the birth of a new star at the heart of the Sayma Nebula. A birth they will be part of! 
To prove to you that I’m right, I’ve shared the asteroid’s co-ordinates with a local captain named Stinger Tash. She assures me I will travel in complete safety with her and her crew.

Official communique of the Imperial Archaeological Division: Control the past, control the future!"
