00AB09BA67D8449F0000031215077FFF,DLAA
00AB09BA67D8449F0000031480DC720C,"Which mode should be used when upscaling graphics to your output resolution.

<color name=""Menu Yellow"">Off:</color> No upscaling will be used and the screen will be rendered at native output resolution.
<color name=""Menu Yellow"">Fixed:</color> Upscaling is based on a fixed rendering resolution to the native output resolution. Which fixed scaling is used, is decided by the scaling quality.
<color name=""Menu Yellow"">Biased:</color> Upscaling which is based on the fixed rendering solution, but in addition biases it towards a 4k output resolution."
00AB09BA67D8449F00000318A98FCC74,Vertical sync
00AB09BA67D8449F0000031985F91F07,"Sync the display of the scene to the refresh rate of the monitor to avoid screen tearing. Turning this option off can increase performance significantly.

<color name=""Menu Yellow"">Off:</color> Does not sync the presenting of frames with the refresh rate of the monitor.
<color name=""Menu Yellow"">On:</color> Sync the presenting of a new frame to the next monitor refresh.
<color name=""Menu Yellow"">Half-rate:</color> Sync the presenting of a new frame to every second monitor refresh.
<color name=""Menu Yellow"">Third-rate:</color> Sync the presenting of a new frame to every third monitor refresh.
<color name=""Menu Yellow"">Quarter-rate:</color> Sync the presenting of a new frame to every fourth monitor refresh."
00AB09BA67D8449F0000031A34F0B5FB,Off
00AB09BA67D8449F0000031BFAC73120,Every frame
00AB09BA67D8449F0000031C2DFCAE60,Half-rate
00AB09BA67D8449F0000031D60B08DFF,Third-rate
00AB09BA67D8449F0000031ED15EB37F,Quarter-rate
